course: dictionary
lesson: 5713
title: Longitude: how far east or west
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Longitude tells you how far east or west a place is. Imagine an invisible line running from the top of the earth to the bottom, through Greenwich in London. Longitude is measured from that line, in degrees.
explain: «Longitude measures how far east or west a place is from the prime meridian.» The prime meridian is the name for the line through Greenwich. Longitude counts from 0° at Greenwich, up to 180°, going either east or west.
explain: Longitude works with latitude. Latitude says how far north or south a place is, and longitude says how far east or west. Together they give a place's exact position, like a map reference.
explain: Lines of longitude are imaginary lines on a map or globe. They run from the North Pole to the South Pole. You cannot see them on the ground, but they help you find any place on Earth.
fact: Longitude is measured in degrees, from 0° at Greenwich up to 180°.
fact: Lines of longitude go from the North Pole to the South Pole.
fact: «Latitude and longitude» together give a place's exact position on a map.
fact: Longitude is linked to time: every 15° is about one hour of time.
fact: Longitude was so hard to measure that ships were wrecked for centuries, until John Harrison's sea clock solved the problem.
exercise: «Longitude measures how far east or west a place is from the prime meridian.» What does longitude measure? | How deep the sea is | How high a mountain is | *How far east or west a place is | How far north or south a place is
exercise: «The equator is a line of latitude, while the prime meridian at Greenwich is a line of longitude.» Which of these is a line of longitude? | The equator | The Arctic Circle | *The prime meridian at Greenwich | The Tropic of Cancer
exercise: Ellie says longitude tells how far north a town is. Is she right? | No, it measures height above sea level | Yes, if the town is near the Equator | *No, longitude measures east or west | Yes, north is what longitude measures
test: Longitude counts from 0° at which place? | The Equator | Cornwall | The North Pole | *Greenwich in London
test: Cornwall lies at about 50° North, 5° West. What does the 5° West tell you? | *How far west of Greenwich it is | How far north it is | How deep under the sea it is | How many hours ahead it is
exam: «Latitude says how far north or south of the Equator a place is, and longitude says how far east or west of Greenwich.» What does longitude tell us? | How far north or south a place is | *How far east or west of Greenwich a place is | The name of a country | The height of a place above sea level
